# 2. Get Specific Module Progress

### Endpoint

```http
GET /progress/:moduleId
```

### Authentication

Required.

### Purpose

Logged-in user ki kisi specific module ki progress retrieve karta hai.

### Example

```http
GET /progress/68b123abc456
```

### Response

```json
{
  "_id": "...",
  "userId": "...",
  "moduleId": {
    "_id": "68b123abc456",
    "title": "Quantum Gates"
  },
  "progress": 75,
  "status": "In Progress"
}
```

`moduleId` ko module ke `title` ke saath populate kiya jata hai.

---

# 3. Get All Module Progress

### Endpoint

```http
GET /progress
```

### Authentication

Required.

### Purpose

Logged-in user ki **saare modules ki progress** retrieve karta hai.

### Example Response

```json
[
  {
    "moduleId": {
      "title": "Introduction to Quantum Computing",
      "order": 1,
      "difficulty": "Beginner"
    },
    "progress": 100,
    "status": "Completed"
  },
  {
    "moduleId": {
      "title": "Quantum Gates",
      "order": 4,
      "difficulty": "Beginner"
    },
    "progress": 60,
    "status": "In Progress"
  }
]
```

Modules ko `order` ke according sort karne ka purpose learning sequence maintain karna hai.

